// Title: Disabled Volume Snapshots
// Sigma ID: dee4af55-1f22-4e1d-a9d2-4bdc7ecb472a
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2021-01-28 | Modified: 2023-12-15
// ATT&CK: defense-impairment, T1685
// Description: Detects commands that temporarily turn off Volume Snapshots
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate administration
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/0gtweet/status/1354766164166115331
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_reg_volsnap_disable.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "\\Services\\VSS\\Diag" and ProcessCommandLine contains "/d Disabled"
